 "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/vercel/jobs/5778418004": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-01-22T11:37:20-05:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "Hybrid - London, Berlin",
  "offices": [
   "EMEA"
  ],
  "salary": null,
  "description": "About Vercel:\n\nVercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what's next. For more than a decade we've helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.\n\nNow we're scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.\n\nAbout The Role:\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Forward-Deployed Engineer to join our Professional Services team. This role is focused on working directly alongside developer teams in our most strategic enterprise customers to drive transformational outcomes across frontend modernization, platform migrations, and AI adoption.\n\nIn this role, you will lead complex Next.js migrations, architect high-performance applications, and build production AI solutions - all within customer environments. You'll work hands-on-keyboard alongside customer teams, whether you're migrating a legacy React application to App Router, conducting a deep-dive code audit, or deploying production agents using Vercel's eve framework and AI SDK.\n\nOur Forward-Deployed Engineers operate with high agency and autonomy. You'll navigate ambiguous enterprise environments, assess technical debt, design migration strategies, and deliver measurable business value - all while building long-term relationships that expand our partnership with each customer.\n\nThere are two main profiles for this role: Next.js experts, and AI builders. Next.js experts work on deep customer code optimization, performance audits, AEO and SEO, and teaching customers how to build Next.js apps with AI instrumentation - such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, etc with Next.js and Vercel agent skills. The AI builder profile is less focused on deep Next.js experience, and more on identifying, evangelizing, and building AI applications and agentic workflows. Your job in this role will be to understand customers’ businesses, scope, design, and build AI agents, and prove their value. The two profiles are not mutually exclusive and we appreciate expertise in both.\n\nYou will report to the Global Manager of Forward Deployed Engineering. This role is remote-first with travel to customer sites expected occasionally. Travel requirements vary, but most of our engineers travel no more than 3-4 days every other month.\n\nWhat You Will Do:\n\n• Build production AI solutions using Vercel's eve framework, AI SDK, and AI Cloud infrastructure, including conversational interfaces, production agents, MCP servers, and agentic workflows that transform customer operations.\n\n• Lead complex frontend migrations - modernizing legacy React, Vue, or other frameworks to Next.js, including Pages to App Router transitions, incremental adoption strategies, and large-scale codebase transformations. Automation of migrations is key to engineering efficiency.\n\n• Conduct code audits and help analyze and improve website performance, analyzing customer codebases for performance bottlenecks, architectural anti-patterns, and optimization opportunities - delivering actionable roadmaps that drive measurable improvements.\n\n• Architect and implement high-performance Next.js applications, leveraging App Router, Server Components, streaming, ISR, and advanced rendering strategies to meet enterprise scale and performance requirements.\n\n• Embed with strategic customers to build production applications - working within their systems, understanding their constraints, and shipping TypeScript code that goes live.\n\n• Drive enablement and knowledge transfer through workshops, pair programming, and documentation - ensuring customer teams can extend and maintain solutions independently.\n\n• Navigate complex enterprise environments by building relationships with stakeholders across engineering, product, and executive teams - translating technical capabilities into business outcomes.\n\n• Contribute to our service evolution by identifying repeatable patterns, building reusable components, and sharing implementation insights back to Product and Engineering teams.\n\nAbout You:\n\n• 6+ years of experience in software engineering with at least 2 years in a customer-facing technical role (consulting, solutions architecture, forward deployed engineering, or technical founder experience).\n\n• Experience using AI instrumentation such as harnesses, skills, and MCPs to build and deploy web applications, backend systems, and/or agentic workflows.\n\n• High agency with comfort in ambiguity - you thrive when given a problem to solve rather than a task to complete, and you can navigate complex organizations to create a plan and drive a project.\n\n• Exceptional communication skills with the ability to conduct technical discovery, present to executives, mentor engineers, and build lasting customer relationships - all with a low-ego, collaborative approach.\n\n• Business acumen to understand customer objectives, translate technical capabilities into ROI, and identify expansion opportunities throughout engagement lifecycles.\n\n• Willingness to travel occasionally to customer sites for embedded work and relationship building.\n\nNext.js-focused Candidates:\n\n• Expert-level TypeScript skills - You are fluent in TypeScript and have strong opinions on type safety, patterns, and tooling.\n\n• Deep expertise in Next.js, with a proven track record of architecting and delivering complex applications using App Router, Server Components, server-side rendering (SSR), static generation (SSG), and incremental static regeneration (ISR), and personalization.\n\n• Demonstrated experience leading frontend migrations - you've converted legacy applications to Next.js, navigated incremental adoption strategies, and understand the challenges of migrating large codebases in production environments.\n\n• Mastery of React and its ecosystem, including advanced state management, performance optimization, and modern patterns like streaming, suspense, and concurrent features.\n\nAI-focused Candidates:\n\n• Production experience with LLMs and AI applications, including agent development, cloud sandbox & filesystem agent patterns, human-in-the-loop patterns, and value optimization. Familiarity with Vercel's eve framework and AI SDK is strongly preferred.\n\n• Ability to identify business cases for AI agents - many customers need guidance not only on how to build AI agents, but where and why to use AI. You’ll need to listen and understand a day-in-the-life of customers’ teams to build proposals.\n\nBonus if you:\n\n• Have led enterprise AI transformation initiatives, including building production agents that automated manual processes or replaced legacy systems.\n\n• Have taught others how to develop software using AI, best practices for building agents, harnesses, skills, and MCPs.\n\n• Have led large-scale migrations from legacy frameworks (Create React App, Gatsby, custom webpack setups) to Next.js in enterprise environments.\n\n• Have expertise in performance optimization and Core Web Vitals, with experience diagnosing and fixing LCP, CLS, and INP issues at scale.\n\n• Have contributed to the Next.js, React, or AI SDK open-source projects, or maintain popular related libraries.\n\n• Have experience with enterprise deployment patterns including security reviews, compliance requirements, and multi-region architectures.\n\n• Have a background in financial services, healthcare, retail/e-commerce, or media - industries with complex frontend ecosystems and growing AI adoption.\n\n• Have spoken at conferences or published thought leadership on frontend architecture, migrations, or AI applications.\n\nBenefits:\n\n• Great compensation package and stock options.\n\n• Inclusive Healthcare Package.\n\n• Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.\n\n• Flexible Time Off - Flexible vacation policy with a recommended 4-weeks per year, and paid holidays.\n\n• Remote Friendly - Work with teammates from different time zones across the globe.\n\n• We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.\n\nDisclosures:\n\n• Privacy: Please review our Job Applicant Privacy Policy for more information on how we handle your data.\n\n• Equal Opportunity: Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don't necessarily check every box on the job description."
 },
 "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/vercel/jobs/5752684004": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-01-07T15:45:38-05:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "Hybrid - San Francisco, New York City, Austin",
  "offices": [
   "Remote - AMER"
  ],
  "salary": null,
  "description": "About Vercel:\n\nVercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what's next. For more than a decade we've helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.\n\nNow we're scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.\n\nAbout the role\n\nAs a Senior Forward-Deployed Engineer on the Professional Services team, you will embed with developer teams at strategic enterprise customers to lead frontend migrations, performance work, and production AI builds. Success looks like production code live in customer environments, customer teams able to extend it on their own, and a wider partnership with each account. This is a remote role open to candidates in the US, with occasional travel to customer sites.\n\nWhat you'll do\n\n• Build production AI agents, Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, and agentic workflows with the AI SDK and the eve framework inside customer environments\n\n• Lead migrations of legacy React, Vue, and other frontends to Next.js, including Pages Router to App Router, and automate the repeatable steps\n\n• Audit customer codebases for performance bottlenecks and architectural anti-patterns, then deliver roadmaps with measurable improvements, including answer engine optimization (AEO) and search engine optimization (SEO)\n\n• Architect and ship high-performance Next.js applications with App Router, Server Components, streaming, and incremental static regeneration (ISR)\n\n• Run workshops and pair programming sessions so customer teams can maintain what you ship, and share repeatable patterns with Product and Engineering\n\nWhat you need\n\n• 6+ years of software engineering experience, including 2+ years in a customer-facing technical role (consulting, solutions architecture, forward-deployed engineering, or technical founder)\n\n• Shipped production TypeScript applications on Next.js and React, including a legacy-to-Next.js migration, or built and deployed production LLM agents with human-in-the-loop patterns and sandboxed execution\n\n• Built and deployed web applications, backend systems, or agentic workflows using AI coding tools such as harnesses, skills, and MCP servers\n\n• Presented technical discovery findings and proposals to executives at enterprise customers, and mentored other engineers\n\nBonus if you\n\n• Led an enterprise AI initiative that replaced a manual process or legacy system with a production agent\n\n• Diagnosed and fixed Core Web Vitals issues (Largest Contentful Paint, Cumulative Layout Shift, Interaction to Next Paint) at scale\n\n• Contributed to Next.js, React, or the AI SDK, or maintain a popular related library\n\nThe San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $137,000.00 - $207,000.00. This salary range is an estimate. Actual salary will be based on job related skills, experience and location. Pay ranges outside San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package also includes benefits and equity-based compensation. Your recruiter can share more about the specific pay range for your location during the hiring process.\n\nDisclosures:\n\n• Privacy: Please review our Job Applicant Privacy Policy for more information on how we handle your data.\n\n• Equal Opportunity: Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don't necessarily check every box on the job description."
 },
 "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/vercel/jobs/6201179004": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-09-22T13:28:34-04:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "Hybrid - San Francisco",
  "offices": [
   "San Francisco, California, United States"
  ],
  "salary": null,
  "description": "About Vercel:\n\nVercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what's next. For more than a decade we've helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.\n\nNow we're scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nWe are looking for a Partner Solutions Engineer to join our partnerships team. This role will drive enablement and integration motions across Vercel's partner ecosystem: solution and consulting partners, strategic technology partners, and cloud alliances such as AWS. Partner Solutions Engineers work with partner engineering, sales, and product teams to grow adoption of Vercel's products and build strong technical relationships.\n\nPartner Solutions Engineers serve as technical collaborators and developer advocates for Vercel's strategic partners. You will work with Vercel's Partner Managers to design and deliver programs such as agentic workshops, discovery sessions, and technical enablement. You will also have the opportunity to work with Vercel's partners on building product integrations and accelerators, bringing them from 0 to 1 and using Vercel, Next.js, AI SDK, and Eve.\n\nPartner Solutions Engineers require a strong web development background, especially in frontend development, cloud infrastructure, agentic development, and modern application development. Strong coordination skills across multiple partners and time zones are essential, as is building lasting relationships with practice leads, delivery teams, and executives.\n\nWhat You Will Do:\n\n• Serve as the main technical contact for Vercel's partners, building lasting relationships with their engineering teams and leadership across solution and consulting partners, technology partners, and cloud alliances.\n\n• Build product integrations, proofs of concept, and reference applications that connect Vercel agentic infrastructure to apps and agents using Vercel’s open source solutions.\n\n• Author the guides, documentation, and workshop content behind Vercel's partner enablement, including integration guides for partner products.\n\n• Provide pre-sales support on partner-attached opportunities.\n\n• Enable Vercel's sales organization on the Vercel + partner better-together story, and present technical content at partner events, hackathons, and conferences.\n\n• Gather and deliver high-signal feedback from partner use cases and integrations to Vercel product teams.\n\nAbout You:\n\n• You are passionate about building first-class web and agent experiences.\n\n• You have a strong understanding of fullstack web architecture, agentic development tools, and building AI applications.\n\n• You have 4+ years of experience as a solutions engineer, solutions architect, or tech lead advising or consulting engineering teams.\n\n• You have 6+ years of experience building and launching frontend applications using Next.js or React, and you still write code regularly.\n\n• You have shipped applications with composable technologies and services common in partner-delivered projects, such as CMS, ecommerce, A/B testing, and personalization.\n\n• You have build and shipped agentic applications with the Vercel AI SDK or other toolkits for AI-powered applications.\n\n• You can speak credibly to LLM frameworks, agent architectures, and AI application patterns.\n\n• You have worked with or within systems integrators, consulting firms, or technology partners, and understand how they staff, deliver, and grow a technology practice or product partnership.\n\n• You are experienced in developer relations, from training sessions and sales demos to conference talks and technical content.\n\n• You have a results-driven mindset and are experienced working in a fast-paced environment.\n\n• You are comfortable working with remote, globally distributed cross-functional teams.\n\n• You have excellent communication skills and experience advising both technical and non-technical stakeholders, from engineers to executives.\n\n• You are able to travel 25% of the time.\n\nBonus if you:\n\n• Have built integrations with Vercel's agentic infrastructure products.\n\n• Have run certification, training, or enablement programs at scale.\n\n• Have experience with cloud marketplace and alliance motions across AWS, Azure, and GCP.\n\n• Have worked at or with a Vercel partner.\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\n• Competitive compensation package, including equity.\n\n• Inclusive Healthcare Package.\n\n• Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.\n\n• Flexible Time Off.\n\n• We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.\n\nThe San Francisco, CA base salary range for this role is $176,000 - $225,000 plus annual bonus. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process. \n\nDisclosures:\n\n• Privacy: Please review our Job Applicant Privacy Policy for more information on how we handle your data.\n\n• Equal Opportunity: Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don't necessarily check every box on the job description."
 },
 "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/vercel/jobs/6132416004": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-08-07T10:36:05-04:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "Hybrid - London, Berlin",
  "offices": [
   "Berlin, Berlin, Germany",
   "London, England, United Kingdom"
  ],
  "salary": null,
  "description": "About Vercel:\n\nVercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what's next. For more than a decade we've helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.\n\nNow we're scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.\n\nAbout the role:\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Partner Solutions Engineer to join our partnerships team in EMEA. This role will lead enablement and pre-sales motions with Vercel's solution and consulting partners (SIs and GSIs) across the region, with a primary focus on the DACH market. Partner Solutions Engineers work with partner engineering, sales, and product teams to grow adoption of Vercel's products and build strong technical relationships.\n\nA key focus in this role will be growing partner-delivered capacity in the DACH region: running Vercel's partner certification program, creating and delivering technical enablement and workshops, and supporting pre-sales motions where partners are engaged. Fluency in German and/or French is essential; this is a spoken, partner-facing role.\n\nThis role will serve as a developer advocate for Vercel across solution and consulting partners. You will be the expert on building and delivering with Vercel products, including AI and agent workloads, and will establish best practices, author guides, lead workshops and hackathons, and build solutions for partner communities and Vercel teams.\n\nPartner Solutions Engineers require a strong web development background, especially in frontend development, cloud infrastructure, networking, and modern application development. Strong coordination skills across multiple partners and time zones are essential, as is building lasting relationships with practice leads, delivery teams, and executives.\n\nThis is an in-person (hybrid) position that will require you to be based in Vercel's London or Berlin office with a required 3 days per week in office. \n\nWhat you will do:\n\n• Serve as subject matter expert on Vercel and Next.js to partner engineering teams and leadership across EMEA.\n\n• Run Vercel's partner certification program in the region: deliver certification workshops, review certification projects, and guide partner engineers through the program.\n\n• Create and deliver technical training and enablement on Next.js and Vercel best practices, including building agents and AI applications on Vercel.\n\n• Deliver one-to-many technical workshops for partner engineering teams, and author the workshop content behind them.\n\n• Run and support partner hackathons that build partner skills and surface joint solutions.\n\n• Provide pre-sales support where partners are engaged: proofs of concept, technical deep dives, and deal unblocking alongside Vercel's sales and sales engineering teams.\n\n• Serve as the main technical contact for SIs and GSIs in the region, building lasting relationships with their engineering teams and practice leadership.\n\n• Build templates and solutions that equip partner communities with the best practices on delivering with Vercel.\n\nAbout you:\n\n• You are passionate about building first-class user experiences on the web.\n\n• You have a strong understanding of web architecture, frontend development, and serverless computing.\n\n• You have 2+ years of experience as a solutions engineer advising or consulting engineering teams.\n\n• You have 4+ years of experience building and launching frontend applications using Next.js or React.\n\n• You speak German and/or French; spoken fluency in at least one of them, alongside professional English, is essential for this role.\n\n• You have worked with or within agencies, systems integrators, or consulting firms, and understand how they staff, deliver, and grow a technology practice.\n\n• You are experienced in developer relations, from training sessions and talks to producing technical content.\n\n• You have a results-driven mindset and are experienced working in a fast-paced environment.\n\n• You are comfortable working with remote, globally distributed cross-functional teams.\n\n• You have excellent communication skills and experience building and maintaining strong relationships with stakeholders.\n\n• You have experience driving the adoption of web technology or previous pre-sales experience.\n\n• You are based in EMEA and able to travel 20% of the time.\n\nBonus if you:\n\n• Have built and shipped AI-powered or agentic applications, ideally with the AI SDK.\n\n• Speak both German and French.\n\n• Have run certification, training, or enablement programs at scale.\n\n• Have experience with composable architectures (headless CMS, commerce, search, analytics) common in partner-delivered projects.\n\nBenefits:\n\n• Competitive compensation package, including equity.\n\n• Inclusive Healthcare Package.\n\n• Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.\n\n• Flexible Time Off.\n\n• We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.\n\nDisclosures:\n\n• Privacy: Please review our Job Applicant Privacy Policy for more information on how we handle your data.\n\n• Equal Opportunity: Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don't necessarily check every box on the job description."
 },
 "https://boards.greenhouse.io/figma/jobs/6158162004?gh_jid=6158162004": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-08-25T17:42:20-04:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "San Francisco, CA • New York, NY • United States",
  "offices": [
   "Canada",
   "US"
  ],
  "salary": {
   "currency": "USD",
   "min": 153000.0,
   "max": 376000.0,
   "unit": "YEAR"
  },
  "description": "Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you're brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you're excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!\n\nFigma is building its founding Forward Deployed Engineering team to solve the complex, real-world challenges that emerge when bringing Figma’s products into large-scale enterprise environments and looking for founding Forward Deployed Engineers. As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you’ll embed directly with strategic customers, working across their codebases, design systems, developer environments, and workflows to make Figma’s products successful within their unique technical constraints. You’ll tackle the hardest adoption challenges hands-on, from complex frontend stacks and legacy systems to security and access requirements, while building trusted partnerships with customers’ senior engineering teams.\n\nThis is a senior/staff-level engineering role within Product and Engineering, not a sales or services function. You’ll work directly in customer environments when needed, using the minimum access required. Your goal is smooth adoption by the customer’s product and engineering teams, which means making complex workflows work simply in their environment and solving the underlying problems You’ll do that hands-on, often by writing Figma product code, then turn what you learn into a reusable path for future customers instead of taking permanent ownership of the customer’s codebase. Working closely with Figma’s Product, Engineering, Sales, and Customer Experience teams, you’ll help shape both the product and how this brand-new function works and scales. The role is highly collaborative, deeply customer-facing, and built for engineers who thrive in ambiguity, take end-to-end ownership, and want to solve the highest-impact problems at the intersection of product, engineering, and customer needs. This role includes periodic travel to work alongside strategic customers in person.\n\nThis is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.\n\nWhat you'll do at Figma:\n\n• Make an enterprise design system agent-ready so AI tools generate faithful, on-system code: fix tokens, naming, and guidelines, wire up Code Connect, and run evals\n\n• Get Make Local, Code Layers, and our newest products working in a customer’s real environment, writing code, config, agent skills, and guideline files against their systems and ours\n\n• Run technical discovery: understand a customer's dev environment, toolchain, and constraints, then scope the fastest credible path to value, in addition to setting the customer up for long term success\n\n• Debug hard, unfamiliar integration problems (git workflows, CI, dev-environment setup, non-standard stacks)\n\n• Build LLM-powered workflows: MCP setup, agent skills, and prompt engineering tuned to each customer’s context\n\n• Turn one-off solutions into reusable playbooks and product feedback, so patterns you solve once become self-serve or shipped product\n\n• Bring learnings on friction back to Figma's Product and Engineering teams, influence what gets built next, and often build it\n\nWe'd love to hear from you if you have:\n\n• 5+ years shipping production software end-to-end, with meaningful time embedded with customers or partner teams\n\n• Excellent customer-facing communication and technical partnership skills, with the ability to build trust with senior engineers and translate customer needs into actionable product and engineering solutions\n\n• Strong engineering fundamentals and adaptability, with the ability to quickly navigate unfamiliar codebases, languages, and technical environments to deliver production-ready solutions\n\n• Hands-on experience with design systems and design-to-code workflows, including component libraries, tokens, documentation, and the tooling that connects design artifacts to production code\n\n• Proficiency in TypeScript/JavaScript or Python, including demonstrated fluency with agentic coding tools (e.g., MCP, agent orchestration). You have hands-on experience integrating APIs and SDKs, troubleshooting toolchains and CI environments, and navigating enterprise requirements such as SSO, security reviews, access controls, data residency, and compliance frameworks\n\n• Comfort owning ambiguous technical problems end to end, identifying patterns across customer engagements, and turning field learning into reusable product improvements\n\nWhile it's not required, it's an added plus if you also have:\n\n• Background in forward-deployed engineering, solutions engineering, professional services, developer experience, or a similar customer-facing technical role\n\n• Familiarity with developer tools, design-to-code workflows, or AI/LLM products, including tools such as Code Connect, Storybook, Style Dictionary, or comparable technologies\n\n• Proven ability to partner cross-functionally with Sales, Customer Experience, Solutions Architecture, or related teams to deliver complex enterprise engagements\n\nAt Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.\n\nPay Transparency Disclosure\n\nJob level and actual compensation will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, individual qualifications objectively assessed during the interview process (including skills and prior relevant experience, potential impact, and scope of role), market demands, and specific work location. \n\nFigma offers equity to employees, as well as a competitive package of additional benefits, including health, dental, and vision coverage; retirement benefits with company contributions; parental leave and reproductive or family planning support; mental health and wellness benefits; and paid time off. Figma provides paid sick leave, holidays, and other leave benefits in compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws, including the requirements of the Washington Minimum Wage Act and related regulations. Exempt employees are eligible for employer‑provided paid flexible PTO in addition to flexible paid sick leave. PTO is subject to manager approval. Additional benefits may include company recharge days, cell phone and home internet reimbursements, and a number of lifestyle spending accounts. Figma also offers sales incentive compensation for most sales roles and an annual bonus plan for eligible non-sales roles. All compensation and benefits are subject to applicable plan terms and may be modified by Figma at any time, consistent with applicable law.\n\nAnnual Base Salary Range:\n$153,000—$376,000 USD\n\nAt Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an equal opportunity workplace - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.\n\nWe will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to accommodations-ext@figma.com. These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities. \n\nExamples of accommodations include but are not limited to: \n\n• Holding interviews in an accessible location\n\n• Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing\n\n• Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers\n\n• Changing the mode or format of interviews \n\nTo ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.\n\nBy applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with Figma's Candidate Privacy Notice.\n\nApplication limits: To help candidates focus on the opportunities most relevant to their skills and experience, Figma limits the number and frequency of applications. These limits apply to all roles:\n\n• Candidates may submit up to 5 applications during any rolling 30-day period.\n\n• Candidates may not reapply to the same role while an application is active or within 90 days of receiving a rejection.\n\nOnce the applicable days has passed, candidates are welcome to apply again."
 },
 "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/gleanwork/jobs/4651990005": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "greenhouse",
  "datePosted": "2026-01-21T14:55:52-05:00",
  "validThrough": null,
  "workplace": null,
  "location_name": "Mountain View, CA",
  "offices": [
   "Mountain View, California, United States",
   "San Francisco, California, United States",
   "US (Remote)"
  ],
  "salary": null,
  "description": "About Glean:\n\nGlean is the Work AI platform that helps everyone work smarter with AI. What began as the industry’s most advanced enterprise search has evolved into a full-scale Work AI ecosystem, powering intelligent Search, an AI Assistant, and scalable AI agents on one secure, open platform. With over 100 enterprise SaaS connectors, flexible LLM choice, and robust APIs, Glean gives organizations the infrastructure to govern, scale, and customize AI across their entire business - without vendor lock-in or costly implementation cycles.\n\nAt its core, Glean is redefining how enterprises find, use, and act on knowledge. Its Enterprise Graph and Personal Knowledge Graph map the relationships between people, content, and activity, delivering deeply personalized, context-aware responses for every employee. This foundation powers Glean’s agentic capabilities - AI agents that automate real work across teams by accessing the industry’s broadest range of data: enterprise and world, structured and unstructured, historical and real-time. The result: measurable business impact through faster onboarding, hours of productivity gained each week, and smarter, safer decisions at every level.\n\nRecognized by Fast Company as one of the World’s Most Innovative Companies (Top 10, 2025), by CNBC’s Disruptor 50, Bloomberg’s AI Startups to Watch (2026), Forbes AI 50, and Gartner’s Tech Innovators in Agentic AI, Glean continues to accelerate its global impact. With customers across 50+ industries and 1,000+ employees in more than 25 countries, we’re helping the world’s largest organizations make every employee AI-fluent, and turning the superintelligent enterprise from concept into reality.\n\nIf you’re excited to shape how the world works, you’ll help build systems used daily across Microsoft Teams, Zoom, ServiceNow, Zendesk, GitHub, and many more. You'll be deeply embedded where people get things done. You'll ship agentic capabilities on an open, extensible stack, with the craft and care required for enterprise trust, as we bring Work AI to every employee, in every company.\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nYou'll join as a founding member of Glean's forward deployed team and operate with the autonomy and accountability of a founder. Your job is to discover and build Glean's next generation of product surfaces, working in a pod with Forward Deployed PMs directly with the C-suite of the world's most influential companies and with Glean's own engineering and product teams.\n\nGlean is a fully horizontal AI platform - and that scope is what makes this role unique. You won't be configuring existing products or optimizing within defined constraints. You'll identify the biggest unsolved business problems at our most strategic customers, build entirely new products to solve them, and in doing so shape what Glean becomes. The best of what you build ships to every Glean customer in the world. You get founder-level ownership with Glean's resources, relationships, and scale behind you.\n\nYou will:\n\n• Discover and build Glean's next product surfaces: Your primary job is 0-to-1 product creation. Nothing about what you're building is predefined - you'll work with your FDPM to identify where Glean's platform can be extended to solve problems no product currently solves, then design and ship it. What you build becomes what Glean ships.\n\n• Lead deep opportunity discovery: Before you write a line of code, you go deep on the business. What's structurally broken? Where is the biggest concentration of unsolved value? What's actually buildable, and what's the fastest path to something real that can be tested and learned from? You'll form strong hypotheses alongside your FDPM and pressure-test them directly with the people who have to live with the outcome.\n\n• Be a technical partner to the C-suite: You'll earn trust at the highest levels of your customer organizations - not just with technical teams, but with the executives who are accountable for outcomes. You can explain what you're building, why it will work, and what the risks are to anyone in the room.\n\n• Scale what works Once something works, you'll make it repeatable - working closely with the core R&D team to ensure the product is scalable\n\n• Stay at the frontier with Glean's R&D team: You'll work closely with Glean's core engineering and product teams, staying ahead of what's possible on the platform and actively shaping how its capabilities evolve. What you encounter in the field directly informs what gets built next.\n\nAbout you:\n\n• You think like a founder. When you walk into a customer, you're curious about the business, digging into what's broken, and figuring out what to build that doesn't yet exist. You're scrappy and resourceful, you move fast enough to learn, and you're as comfortable in a strategic discussion with a CEO as you are deep in a codebase. You've shipped actual products that real people use, that drove real outcomes - and you want to do it at a higher level of ambition.\n\n• 0-to-1 build track record: You've built production software from scratch in ambiguous environments. You can point to something that didn't exist before you showed up and is now used by real people at scale.\n\n• Production AI experience: You've shipped AI-powered solutions in the real world - prompt engineering, agent development, evaluation frameworks, deployment at scale. Not just prototypes.\n\n• Full-stack technical depth: Strong programming skills across the stack with a deep understanding of and experience with how enterprise systems actually work.\n\n• Business acumen: You can walk into a customer, identify where the real problems are, and connect that diagnosis to a product hypothesis - without being handed a brief.\n\n• Customer instinct: You build trust quickly at every level of an organization, communicate with clarity, and know how to tailor your depth to the room.\n\n• Builder's judgment: You know what's actually buildable, how long it will take, and when to simplify scope to get something real into production faster. You spot problems early and solve them independently.\n\n• Curiosity and scrappiness: You're driven to understand problems deeply before solving them, and resourceful enough to find a path forward when none is obvious.\n\n• Experience: 4+ years in technical roles with a track record of shipping production software. Former technical founders are strongly encouraged to apply.\n\n• Willingness to travel: This role requires 25–50% travel.\n\n• Nice to Have:\n\n• Experience as a founder, at a top-tier technology company, or in a forward deployed engineering role.\n\n• A technical degree in CS, engineering, math, or a related field.\n\n• Deep familiarity with LLMs, retrieval systems, and evaluation frameworks.\n\n• Experience driving technology adoption inside large enterprises.\n\nLocation: \n\n• This role is hybrid (3-4 days a week in one of our SF Bay Area offices)\n\n• This role requires 25-50% travel\n\nCompensation & Benefits:\n\nThe standard range for this position is $160,000-$270,000 annually. Compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for variable compensation, equity, and benefits. Special Note: This range encompasses varying levels of the role, you will be assessed for your level during the interview process.\n\nWe offer a comprehensive benefits package including competitive compensation, Medical, Vision, and Dental coverage, generous time-off policy, and the opportunity to contribute to your 401k plan to support your long-term goals. When you join, you'll receive a home office improvement stipend, as well as an annual education and wellness stipends to support your growth and wellbeing. We foster a vibrant company culture through regular events, and provide healthy lunches daily to keep you fueled and focused.\n\nWe are a diverse bunch of people and we want to continue to attract and retain a diverse range of people into our organization. We're committed to an inclusive and diverse company. We do not discriminate based on gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, civil or family status, age, disability, or race.\n\n#LI-HYBRID\n\nAI-First Mindset at Glean:\n\nAt Glean, AI fluency is core to how we work and we're committed to ensuring every new hire feels confident integrating AI into their everyday work. As part of the interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about, design, and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today — prior Glean experience isn't required.\n\nGlobal Data Privacy Notice for Job Candidates and Applicants:\n\nDepending on your location, the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), or other privacy laws may regulate the way we manage the data of job applicants. Our full notice outlining how data will be processed as part of the application procedure for applicable locations is available in our Privacy Policy. By submitting your application, you are agreeing to our use and processing of your data as required. US applicants and their applications are subject to arbitration of disputes as outlined in our Applicant Arbitration Agreement.\n\nBy clicking “Submit Application,” I confirm that I have read the Global Data Privacy Notice and the Applicant Arbitration Agreement, and I agree to the terms."
 },
