   "min": 189000,
   "max": 330000,
   "unit": "YEAR"
  },
  "description": "ABOUT RAMP\n\nRamp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $200B in annualized spend flows in and out of 70,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books.\n\nThe problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving.\n\nWe hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome.\n\nThe median Ramp customer saves 5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same.\n\nIf you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Forward Deployed, you’ll solve the hardest problems standing between Ramp and the world’s largest and most complex companies — shaping and shipping the product capabilities that unlock our growth upmarket. You'll be part of our Core FDE org, which is an agent-first, high-pace, customer-facing engineering team. On FDE, you will interact directly with customers and deliver solutions end to end — understanding pain points, shaping product decisions, and building agents that autonomously expand Ramp's capabilities.\n\nCheck out our Engineering Blog https://engineering.ramp.com/ and FDE post https://engineering.ramp.com/post/forward-deployed-engineering for more context on our work!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Deliver software end to end that meet the needs of our largest customers — understanding user pain points, scoping product specs, and building agents that autonomously implement solutions.\n\n - Collaborate closely with Sales, Solutions, Customer Success, and Account Management to close deals, activate customers, and expand the value Ramp provides over time.\n\n - Drive the core product engineering roadmap through our embedding model — specializing within a core product area to develop deep domain expertise and make prioritization calls on when to build a custom solution vs. accelerate a broader initiative.\n\n\nWHAT YOU NEED\n\n - 3+ years of software engineering experience preferred\n\n - Extensive experience building with and for agents\n\n - Track record of shipping high-quality products at scale\n\n - Comfort and excitement to be customer-facing\n\n - Desire to work in a fast-paced environment, continuously grow, and master your craft\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS AVAILABLE TO ALL FULL-TIME RAMP EMPLOYEES (GLOBAL)\n\n - Flexible PTO\n\n - Centralized home-office equipment ordering\n\n - Health and wellness stipend\n\n - Budget for intra-office travel\n\n - Weekly coffee stipend\n\n\n\n\nUNITED STATES\n\n - 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents\n\n - One Medical annual membership\n\n - 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp\n\n - Fertility HRA (up to $10,000 per year)\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay\n\n - Pet insurance\n\n - In-office perks: lunch, snacks, drinks, and more\n\n - Relocation expense coverage to NYC or SF (if needed)\n   \n   \n\n\nCANADA\n\n - Group medical, dental, and vision coverage through Sun Life\n\n - Life, AD&D, and disability coverage\n\n - Fertility drug coverage (up to $4,000 lifetime)\n\n - Group Retirement Plan with employer match (RRSP + DPSP)\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay, with additional time available at reduced pay\n\n - Employee Assistance Program and virtual care through Lumino Health\n\n\n\n\nUNITED KINGDOM\n\n - Private medical insurance through Freedom Elite\n\n - Virtual GP and at-home care via eMed x Livi\n\n - Workplace pension through Penfold, with salary sacrifice option\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay with additional time available at reduced pay\n\n\n\n\nREFERRAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nIf you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf.\n\n \n\n\nOTHER NOTICES\n\nPursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n \n\nBeware of recruiting scams: Ramp will only contact you through official @Ramp.com http://Ramp.com email addresses and will never ask for payment or sensitive personal information during the hiring process.\n\n \n\nRamp Applicant Privacy Notice https://ramp.com/legal/applicant-privacy-notice"
 },
 "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ramp/8efd3a0a-fc66-46e2-9415-bffba10e2919": {
  "fetched": "2026-10-17T05:46:45+00:00",
  "live": true,
  "source": "ashby",
  "datePosted": "2026-08-27T03:05:26.969+00:00",
  "workplace": "Hybrid",
  "employmentType": "FullTime",
  "addresses": [
   {
    "addressRegion": "NY",
    "addressCountry": "USA",
    "addressLocality": "New York City"
   }
  ],
  "salary": {
   "currency": "USD",
   "min": 217000,
   "max": 298000,
   "unit": "YEAR"
  },
  "description": "ABOUT RAMP\n\nRamp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $200B in annualized spend flows in and out of 70,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books.\n\nThe problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving.\n\nWe hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome.\n\nThe median Ramp customer saves 5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same.\n\nIf you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nRamp is building a new AI business, and you’ll be one of its first technical sellers. Your job is to turn technically complex AI products into closed revenue.\n\nYou’ll sell a growing portfolio spanning AI-powered applications and agents for finance teams, as well as infrastructure that helps companies deploy and manage AI with greater control, security, and cost efficiency. This is a product-focused, quota-carrying technical sales role. You’ll help customers evaluate and purchase Ramp’s AI products, translating complex capabilities into clear business value and guiding opportunities from discovery through close.\n\nThis is a high-velocity commercial role, not a traditional pre-sales position where success ends with a great demo. You’ll be accountable for turning technical evaluations into commercial wins from start to finish. You’ll lead discovery, shape deal strategy, build executive-level business cases, deliver tailored demonstrations, navigate technical and commercial objections, and create urgency around a clear path to purchase.\n\nYou’ll move comfortably between technical and executive conversations. In one meeting, you may discuss model routing, APIs, integrations, data governance, and security with Engineering and IT teams. In the next, you may help Finance and executive leaders understand the ROI, total cost of ownership, and operational impact of adopting Ramp’s AI products.\n\nYou’ll join at a formative moment for Ramp’s AI business. As one of the first dedicated sellers for these products, you’ll help identify the strongest use cases, refine how we position and sell the portfolio, influence the customer experience, and build the playbook the broader team will eventually scale. You’ll own the full customer lifecycle from discovery and evaluation through close, implementation, and adoption, helping customers translate their purchase into a successful deployment. This role combines Ramp’s resources and customer reach with the ownership, speed, and ambiguity of an early-stage team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Carry a revenue quota and own the progression of AI product opportunities from initial discovery through purchase, ensuring business value is clear, technical requirements are validated, and obstacles to a decision are resolved.\n\n - Lead discovery with business and technical buyers to understand their goals, workflows, challenges, decision criteria, existing systems, and AI strategy.\n\n - Translate Ramp’s AI applications and infrastructure into compelling solution narratives tied to measurable business outcomes.\n\n - Build ROI and total cost of ownership analyses that quantify the value of Ramp’s AI products and create executive-level justification for investment.\n\n - Help customers identify high-value use cases, set realistic expectations, and establish a credible path from evaluation to production.\n\n - Deliver tailored demonstrations, technical workshops, and proofs of concept with clear success criteria that establish value and build confidence in a purchase decision.\n\n - Build relationships with champions and decision-makers across Engineering, IT, Security, Finance, Operations, Procurement, and executive leadership.\n\n - Navigate questions related to APIs, integrations, model capabilities and limitations, data flows, architecture, privacy, security, governance, implementation, and tradeoffs among quality, cost, latency, and control.\n\n - Apply strong commercial judgment to qualify opportunities, create urgency, address objections, identify risk, and keep customers moving toward a decision.\n\n - Lead customers through implementation after purchase, including deployment planning, stakeholder alignment, workflow design, technical coordination, enablement, and adoption.\n\n - Partner with Account Executives and collaborate with Product, Engineering, Security, Marketing, and post-sales teams to remove deployment blockers and deliver a strong customer experience from evaluation through production.\n\n - Bring structured customer and market feedback to internal teams to improve the products, positioning, sales execution, and customer experience.\n\n - Turn early customer conversations into repeatable messaging, demonstrations, qualification criteria, value stories, and sales plays as we build this go-to-market motion from the ground up.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BRING\n\n - 5+ years of experience in Solutions Engineering, Solutions Consulting, technical sales, Solutions Architecture, enterprise software sales, or a related customer-facing role.\n\n - Direct quota-carrying or deal-closing ownership of the pre-sale cycle—not only experience delivering demonstrations or supporting post-sale implementation.\n\n - A track record of independently influencing and winning complex B2B sales opportunities with clear revenue accountability.\n\n - Strong discovery and value-selling skills, with the ability to connect technical capabilities to measurable business outcomes.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build executive-level business cases, including ROI and total cost of ownership analyses; this capability will be central to success in the role.\n\n - Commercial instincts and comfort taking meaningful ownership of deal strategy, momentum, and results.\n\n - Technical fluency across modern AI systems, including applications and agents, model capabilities and limitations, APIs, integrations, data flows, security, governance, and tradeoffs among quality, cost, latency, and control.\n\n - Excellent executive communication and presentation skills, including the ability to make complex concepts clear and relevant to different audiences.\n\n - The ability to explain probabilistic, rapidly evolving AI technology with credibility and precision without overpromising what the product can do.\n\n - Experience building champions and navigating multi-threaded buying groups with competing priorities.\n\n - High ownership, curiosity, sound judgment, and comfort operating in a fast-moving environment where you’ll build structure as you go rather than inherit it.\n\n - Energy for zero-to-one work and the opportunity to build a sales motion rather than simply inherit one.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience selling AI infrastructure, AI applications or agents, developer tools, data platforms, security products, finance technology, or workflow automation software.\n\n - Experience helping launch a new product or develop an early go-to-market motion.\n\n - Familiarity with AI gateways, model routing, usage controls, data governance, or enterprise AI deployment.\n\n - Experience selling to developers, IT, Security, Finance, Operations, Procurement, or executive stakeholders.\n\n - Experience creating reusable sales assets, demonstrations, value frameworks, or enablement programs.\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS AVAILABLE TO ALL FULL-TIME RAMP EMPLOYEES (GLOBAL)\n\n - Flexible PTO\n\n - Centralized home-office equipment ordering\n\n - Health and wellness stipend\n\n - Budget for intra-office travel\n\n - Weekly coffee stipend\n\n\n\n\nUNITED STATES\n\n - 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents\n\n - One Medical annual membership\n\n - 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp\n\n - Fertility HRA (up to $10,000 per year)\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay\n\n - Pet insurance\n\n - In-office perks: lunch, snacks, drinks, and more\n\n - Relocation expense coverage to NYC or SF (if needed)\n   \n   \n\n\nCANADA\n\n - Group medical, dental, and vision coverage through Sun Life\n\n - Life, AD&D, and disability coverage\n\n - Fertility drug coverage (up to $4,000 lifetime)\n\n - Group Retirement Plan with employer match (RRSP + DPSP)\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay, with additional time available at reduced pay\n\n - Employee Assistance Program and virtual care through Lumino Health\n\n\n\n\nUNITED KINGDOM\n\n - Private medical insurance through Freedom Elite\n\n - Virtual GP and at-home care via eMed x Livi\n\n - Workplace pension through Penfold, with salary sacrifice option\n\n - Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay with additional time available at reduced pay\n\n\n\n\nREFERRAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nIf you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf.\n\n \n\n\nOTHER NOTICES\n\nPursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n \n\nBeware of recruiting scams: Ramp will only contact you through official @Ramp.com http://Ramp.com email addresses and will never ask for payment or sensitive personal information during the hiring process.\n\n \n\nRamp Applicant Privacy Notice https://ramp.com/legal/applicant-privacy-notice"
 },
